# Prettier owns formatting for every file type it supports in this project:
# Markdown, JavaScript, JSON, YAML, HTML and CSS. `bin/prettier --check .` runs
# in CI (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# This file is nearly empty on purpose. Prettier 3 defaults --ignore-path to
# ['.gitignore', '.prettierignore'], so everything git already ignores
# (node_modules/, app/assets/builds/, public/assets/, tmp/, log/, storage/) is
# skipped without repeating it here. Files Prettier has no parser for (.rb,
# .erb, .lock, Gemfile) are skipped automatically too.
#
# Add an entry below only for a file that is tracked in git, has a Prettier
# parser, and still should not be reformatted.
